 "news": {
  "date": "2026-10-12",
  "asof": "2026-10-13 12:27 UTC",
  "headline": "Crude jumps 3.3% while the tape does nothing \u2014 and the bond market was shut on the eve of CPI",
  "standfirst": "The only move on the board was oil. WTI settled $93.74, up 3.28%, and Brent $106.65, on renewed Russian strikes on Ukrainian energy infrastructure and fresh attacks on tankers in the Strait of Hormuz \u2014 two sessions after Trump ruled out an American attack on Iran before the midterms, which is the point: this market prices interruption to flow, not Washington. Equities offset to nothing, the S&P \u22120.06% to 7,807.24 on a four-point change, the Dow +0.38%, the Nasdaq \u22120.44% and the Russell \u22120.45%, and Treasuries did not trade for Columbus Day. In the book GOOG made a new closing high at 348.97 and AAPL rose 1.29% to 340.97, undoing Friday\u2019s order-cut fall in a single session, while OKTA opened at a 52-week high of 235.00 and closed 227.08, down 2.18% \u2014 a net of +0.39 on the day. Heat 3.05R against 3.0R, unchanged for a twenty-third session. September CPI lands tomorrow.",
  "themes": [
   {
    "kicker": "What's next",
    "right": "CPI and the banks on Tuesday \u00b7 then 28 October",
    "title": "The print the fortnight has been building toward lands tomorrow",
    "items": [
     {
      "tone": "c-cb",
      "tag": "CPI",
      "html": "<b>September CPI</b> \u2014 the only first-tier print before the Fed, and the arbiter of two ISM prices indices against a soft PCE",
      "when": "Tue \u00b7 2026-10-13",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-er",
      "tag": "BANKS",
      "html": "<b>Citigroup, JPMorgan Chase and Wells Fargo</b> \u2014 the first read on credit, loan demand and the consumer this quarter",
      "when": "Tue \u00b7 2026-10-13",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-fomc",
      "tag": "FOMC",
      "html": "<b>Fed decision</b> \u2014 the minutes promise another hike; the market prices roughly a 78% hold",
      "when": "Wed \u00b7 2026-10-28",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-cb",
      "tag": "GOOG",
      "html": "<b>Alphabet Q3 earnings</b> \u2014 $195-205bn of capex and 3.6GW of contracted power, into an AI funding scare",
      "when": "Wed \u00b7 2026-10-28",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-cb",
      "tag": "AAPL",
      "html": "<b>Apple Q4 earnings</b> \u2014 the first iPhone 18 quarter, now against an order-cut report, and the first read on Ternus",
      "when": "Thu \u00b7 2026-10-29",
      "kind": "calendar"
     }
    ],
    "note": "<b>September CPI has to settle three arguments that have run all fortnight.</b> Whether the ISM prices indices at <b>77.9</b> and <b>74.0</b> are feeding through or stalling at the factory gate, when core PCE came in at <b>3.0% against 3.3%</b>. Whether the Fed's minutes and Waller's comments describe a committee that will hike or one that is talking. And whether the long end's behaviour is inflation or supply \u2014 where Thursday's auction and Friday's flattening are the only two pieces of evidence against the supply story, and a hot print washes them both away. The bond market has not traded since Friday, so it reacts to three days of thinking at once."
   }
  ],
  "ondeck": "<b>September CPI has to settle three arguments that have run all fortnight.</b> Whether the ISM prices indices at <b>77.9</b> and <b>74.0</b> are feeding through or stalling at the factory gate, when core PCE came in at <b>3.0% against 3.3%</b>. Whether the Fed's minutes and Waller's comments describe a committee that will hike or one that is talking. And whether the long end's behaviour is inflation or supply \u2014 where Thursday's auction and Friday's flattening are the only two pieces of evidence against the supply story, and a hot print washes them both away. The bond market has not traded since Friday, so it reacts to three days of thinking at once.",
